<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia's affilates to get 2.32 mln bls Sep LSWR.</title>
<headline>Indonesia's affilates to get 2.32 mln bls Sep LSWR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned Pertamina is expected to allocate 2.32 million barrels of low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) out of its total September allocation of 3.6 million barrels to its affilliates, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the 2.32 million barrels, Perta is expected to be allotted 560,000 barrels, Far East Investment 540,000 barrels, Pacific Petroleum 300,000 barrels, Korean Indonesian Petroleum Co 120,000 barrels and Indoil 800,000 barrels.</p>
</text>
